        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Dichloromethane (3 mL) was added to 10 mL of a methanol/acetonitrile mixture (v/v = 4/1) containing H3L (0.025 mmol) and Nd(dbm)3·2H2O (0.025 mmol). The mixture was stirred for about 1 h at room temperature, then sealed in a 20 mL glass vial and heated at 75 °C for 72 h. The temperature was slowly decreased to room temperature. The mixture was washed with cold methanol, yielding yellow block-shaped crystals.",
